sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-23> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Universality proofs proceed by building components from localized structures, which requires controlled transmission of information; in class 3 systems a change to a single cell eventually spreads to all cells, making it very hard to identify definite components and hence to prove universality.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Uncontrolled information flow in class 3 rules hinders universality proofs";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “The Threshold of Universality in Cellular Automata” (from p. 694), p. 698. Scope: class 3 cellular automata and methods for proving universality"
}
